# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: optimization -- what DEBUG / SPACE / SPEED decide, and clal-compile-system
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: design
#+DEPENDS: compiler
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-11-04

"SPACE reads back but drives nothing on its own. Only DEBUG decides
instrumentation; the matrix's SPACE x column confirms that's intended,
so SPACE is currently a value you can store and retrieve."

==> actually, it should be the relative value of the optimization
levels that determines the effect:


| example levels                | non-instrumented fork          | instrumented fork                                         |
|-------------------------------+--------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------|
| (DEBUG 3) (SPACE x) (SPEED 0) | present, SPEED<1:  interpreted | DEBUG>=SPACE: present instrumented, SPEED<2:  interpreted |
| (DEBUG 3) (SPACE x) (SPEED 3) | present, SPEED>=1: compiled    | DEBUG>=SPACE: present instrumented, SPEED>=2: compiled    |
| (DEBUG 0) (SPACE 3) (SPEED 0) | present, SPEED<1:  interpreted | DEBUG<SPACE:  absent                                      |
| (DEBUG 0) (SPACE 3) (SPEED 3) | present, SPEED>=1: compiled    | DEBUG<SPACE:  absent                                      |

So: 

interpreted = SPEED<1
compiled    = SPEED>=1
instrumented fork present = DEBUG>=SPACE
instrumented fork absent  = DEBUG<SPACE

non-instrumented fork present = always true

And this leaves some space for different (intermediary) levels of optimization, such as, indeed:
SPEED level is the threshold — 0 means never, 1 and 2 keep the hotness threshold, 3 means compile eagerly at definition.
This means that with SPEED 1 and 2, we get compilation on demand (and therefore optimization can only occur per function, like with CLAL-COMPILE).
While with SPEED 3, we compile the whole file at once during LOAD, and therefore we can perform file-wide optimizations.

Note, in Common Lisp implementations this can be archived by the use of:

#+begin_src lisp
(with-compilation-unit (:override t) #|for each transformed defun in the file:|# (compile name lambda) …)
#+end_src

For system-wide (global) optimizations, we could compile several files in one unit with:
#+begin_src lisp
(with-compilation-unit (:override nil) (compile-file path) …)
#+end_src

For now, we don't provide an "application" or "system" compilation
function like bricscad when we generate a .des or autocad with a .vlx,
but we could with:

#+begin_src lisp
(clal-compile-system list-of-files)
#+end_src
that would be implemented as:
#+begin_src lisp
(with-compilation-unit (:override nil) (dolist (file list-of-files) (clal-compile-file file) …))
#+end_src

But if we had (DEBUG 3) (SPEED 0) (SPACE 0) while calling clal-compile-system
we would have to do just:
#+begin_src lisp
(dolist (file list-of-files) (clal-compile-file file) …)
#+end_src

and clal-compile-file similarly would do just:
#+begin_src lisp
  #|for each transformed defun in the file:|# (compile name lambda)
#+end_src

to avoid the global optimizations (eg. coalesing of common literal
data structures, direct linking of functions (instead of going thru
the symbol binding), etc.

One optimization Briscad does, with high level optimization, is to
detect whether a local variable is a free variable or a bound variable
in the function, and when bound, transform it into essentially a
lexical binding instead of a dynamic binding. (Unfortunately the test
is imperfect, so this can be detected when we call functions using
dynamically these variables! In that case we must disable this
failling optimization in bricscad).

So now we may implement clal-compile, clal-compile-file,
vlisp-compile-file (same as clal-compile-file with a different API
IIRC), Let's add (clal-compile-system output-file source-file-list)

Note: with-compilation-unit defers warning about undefined
functions. So we may have forward definitions even across files.



* Resolved (implemented by the compiler epic; closed 2026-11-04)

Re-added to issues/open/ on 2026-11-04; every point is in the tree:

- the levels: the non-instrumented fork is always present, compiled at
  SPEED >= 1; the instrumented fork is present while DEBUG >= SPACE and
  compiled at SPEED >= 2; SPEED 3 compiles eagerly at definition, a whole
  file in one unit (clautolisp --help, -O; user manual, Optimization;
  RELEASE_NOTES, "kept while DEBUG >= SPACE");
- clal-compile, clal-compile-file, vlisp-compile and clal-compile-system
  (one host compilation unit: literals coalesced across files, forward
  references resolve) -- autolisp-compiler/source/compile-file.lisp,
  tests in clal-extensions-tests.lisp, manual sections CLAL-COMPILE-FILE /
  CLAL-COMPILE-SYSTEM;
- the BricsCAD-style "bound local becomes lexical" optimization is the
  lexical-locals fork (compile-function.lisp, with its whole-corpus CI
  lane); a function whose lambda list names *ERROR* gets no lexical fork
  (local-error-handler-not-called, 2.3.28).
